# chezmoi:modify-template
{{- /*
Merge the managed MCP server entry into Pi's existing ~/.pi/agent/mcp.json
instead of replacing it, so servers added with `pi mcp add` survive
`chezmoi apply`.

- `mcpServers.home-assistant` is chezmoi-managed and always wins, the same way
  `theme` wins in settings.json. Runtime changes to *this* entry (exposure
  toggled from `/mcp`) are therefore reverted on the next apply; change the
  entry here instead. Other servers, and any top-level keys, are preserved
  untouched.
- The URL is the Home Assistant Cloud remote UI host, not the
  home.opsgoodness.net custom domain. HA only advertises a canonical external
  URL for the instance whose host matches its own configuration, and for any
  other host its OAuth metadata comes back with relative endpoints and no
  `issuer`, which a conforming client must reject ("Invalid authorization
  server issuer"). Cloud is also reachable from anywhere, so the server needs
  no LAN access and no macOS Local Network permission for Rex.
- `clientRegistration: "cimd"` is required: HA advertises
  `client_id_metadata_document_supported` and has no RFC 7591 dynamic client
  registration, so Pi's default registration fails.
- `exposure: "direct"` declares HA's ~22 tools to the model instead of
  reaching them through codemode scripts, which suits a server used for
  one-step device control.
- OAuth credentials live in ~/.pi/agent/mcp-auth.json, which stays unmanaged:
  they are per-machine, and `pi mcp login home-assistant` is how a machine
  gets them.
*/ -}}
{{- $current := dict -}}
{{- if trim .chezmoi.stdin -}}
{{-   $current = fromJson .chezmoi.stdin -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- $servers := index $current "mcpServers" | default dict -}}
{{- $_ := set $servers "home-assistant" (dict
      "url" "https://nlnxn14gitl4kd5tloexvihlfzxnewdb.ui.nabu.casa/api/mcp"
      "description" "Home Assistant: query and control lights, switches, climate, scenes, media players and all other exposed entities."
      "exposure" "direct"
      "oauth" (dict "clientRegistration" "cimd")) -}}
{{- $_ := set $current "mcpServers" $servers -}}
{{- toPrettyJson $current -}}
